      {
        "id": 221267,
        "name": "Blackfang108",
        "username": "Blackfang108",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-08-15T18:41:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That’s your choice if you want a different team but that changes nothing about my point.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Doesn't mean I have to like it.</p>\n<p>It doesn't make my chief complaints about the randomized one-shots go away. (that it's impossible to have a real discussion about the one-shot itself when it's random).</p>\n<p>And it doesn't make it any less frustrating to have every. single. randomized one-shot starts me off with a hand that's about as bad as possible for each character, and not have a chance of winning, only to have a bunch of people come out with \"Easy mint.\"&nbsp; I don't begruge them their luck, but that doesn't mean I have to like mine.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:53:54.463Z",
